    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26502" root="طرأ" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مطرئ</span></b>  [thus written, without any syll. signs,
in the TA, and there said to be the subst. (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْم</span>)
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَطْرَأَهُ</span>: but I think that it is evidently
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُطْرِئٌ</span>; and not the subst., but the act. part. n.
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْمُ الفَاعِلِ</span>), of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَطْرَأَهُ</span>].

